id: pm-gh1413
title: "GH-1413: Preserve lossless producer cursors under amount-only output caps"
description: "Rebase advertised list/search producer continuation after the last delivered row when an explicit output amount cap binds but the token budget does not. Preserve combined ceilings, deletion fallback, strict read truth and public SDK/CLI compatibility."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-06T09:32:33.780Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-06T11:49:33.463Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-06T11:49:32.857Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-06T11:49:32.857Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: Exact ordered CLI and public SDK list/search traversal with producer limit25 and output-limit2 under unbounded and high finite budgets; no skipped or repeated IDs; truthful terminal counts and deliberate caps; preserve combined-ceiling and deletion-fallback controls; exact coverage and packed Node/Bun/npx/bunx acceptance.
parent: pm-5t33or
risk: medium
confidence: 90
resolution: Rebase advertised producer continuation after amount-only projection.
expected_result: List and search cursors resume after the final delivered row when an amount cap binds without token compaction; composed amount/token rebasing remains lossless and explicit terminal caps retain deliberate-partial semantics.
actual_result: All 15 linked producer/consumer cases pass with exact ordered traversal and both runtime exports; real installed Node and Bun consumers each traverse 30 rows with four amount-only cases and no skips or duplicates. Exact full-source coverage is100/100/100/100 and all local mandatory gates pass; exact-head hosted admission is required before merge.
